WEBVTT

1
00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.291
<b>Here begins</b>

2
00:00:52.291 --> 00:00:56.583
<b>the third chapter of the Gita, "Karma Yoga,"</b>

3
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:58.666
<b>And it starts with</b>

4
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:01.333
<b>Arjuna's confusion.</b>

5
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.416
<b>Arjuna says:</b>

6
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:04.875
<b>"hey Keshav</b>

7
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:06.541
<b>hey Janardhan,</b>

8
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:09.583
<b>if wisdom and knowledge is superior to action,</b>

9
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:14.708
<b>then why do you urge me </b>
<b>to engage in this brutal war?</b>

10
00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:19.250
<b>Your seemingly contradictory </b>
<b>words are confusing me.</b>

11
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:28.083
<b>I beg you, suggest a clear and </b>
<b>a certain path that's best for me."</b>

12
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:32.125
<b>Arjuna's distress is natural and understandable.</b>

13
00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.375
<b>Let's further understand this.</b>

14
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:44.083
<b>Arjuna is struggling to </b>
<b>understand what he should do.</b>

15
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:46.041
<b>In the second chapter,</b>

16
00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:49.166
<b>Krishna shared various teachings.</b>

17
00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:50.708
<b>For instance,</b>

18
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:53.833
<b>In the verse 49,</b>

19
00:01:53.833 --> 00:02:00.375
<b>he advised Arjuna to take refuge </b>
<b>in wisdom and knowledge,</b>

20
00:02:00.375 --> 00:02:06.166
<b>rising above all the selfish actions, </b>
<b>and keeping them away.</b>

21
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:07.083
<b>Yet,</b>

22
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:11.875
<b>in other verses, Krishna encourages Arjuna </b>
<b>to fight the war. </b>

23
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:14.166
<b>He suggests that for Arjuna,</b>

24
00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>engaging in this battle while rooted in </b>
<b>spiritual wisdom is the right course of action.</b>

25
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:26.375
<b>Arjuna sees a contradiction in Krishna's words</b>

26
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:28.000
<b>and feels bewildered.</b>

27
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.041
<b>Because,</b>

28
00:02:29.041 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>to him, this war seems like a lowly act.</b>

29
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:41.208
<b>If divine knowledge and wisdom are to be sought,</b>

30
00:02:41.208 --> 00:02:45.041
<b>Then why is Krishna pushing him to fight?</b>

31
00:02:45.041 --> 00:02:51.875
<b>How can a violent activity like war be better </b>
<b>than the non-violence of supreme knowledge?</b>

32
00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:53.416
<b>The truth is,</b>

33
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:58.458
<b>Arjuna isn't fully grasping Krishna's teachings,</b>

34
00:02:58.458 --> 00:03:03.583
<b>which is why he's openly expressing his doubts.</b>

35
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:10.958
<b>He's asking Krishna to suggest a </b>
<b>definite path that would be best for him.</b>

36
00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:11.875
<b>Perhaps</b>

37
00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:18.166
<b>we would also have such similar questions </b>
<b>and confusions in our mind.</b>

38
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:19.291
<b>Shri Krishna</b>

39
00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:22.333
<b>will address these concerns in this chapter.</b>

40
00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:30.708
<b>I’m sure even you must be </b>
<b>having doubts in your mind.</b>

41
00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:32.125
<b>it's natural.</b>

42
00:03:32.125 --> 00:03:34.083
<b>For a worldly person,</b>

43
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:40.458
<b>understanding this divine knowledge</b>
<b>can be challenging</b>

44
00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:43.541
<b>and may also take time.</b>

45
00:03:43.541 --> 00:03:44.500
<b>Here,</b>

46
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.333
<b>Arjuna is in a similar situation.</b>

47
00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:53.916
<b>This state of confusion is undoubtedly painful.</b>

48
00:03:53.916 --> 00:03:59.708
<b>And if the answers further</b>
<b>complicate rather than clarify,</b>

49
00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:02.708
<b>confusing the person even more,</b>

50
00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:08.416
<b>it becomes extremely distressing</b>
<b>for their intellect.</b>

51
00:04:08.416 --> 00:04:13.166
<b>In personal life, we often </b>
<b>encounter such situations</b>

52
00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:18.833
<b>where we see contradictions in others' words,</b>

53
00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:24.958
<b>unable to understand what </b>
<b>they're trying to convey.</b>

54
00:04:24.958 --> 00:04:28.416
<b>This is quite common.</b>

55
00:04:28.416 --> 00:04:29.916
<b>But</b>

56
00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:30.916
<b>in such cases,</b>

57
00:04:30.916 --> 00:04:36.500
<b>many people's egos get hurt,</b>

58
00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.250
<b>and this ego,</b>

59
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:47.458
<b>tries to prove the other person wrong </b>
<b>without understanding their perspective.</b>

60
00:04:47.458 --> 00:04:53.291
<b>Sometimes, people don't even hesitate</b>
<b>to make personal attacks.</b>

61
00:04:53.291 --> 00:04:58.291
<b>A simple discussion turns into an argument,</b>

62
00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:01.875
<b>and the argument into tension.</b>

63
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:05.458
<b>Nobody wins in this scenario,</b>

64
00:05:05.458 --> 00:05:11.333
<b>but knowledge certainly loses.</b>

65
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:13.875
<b>Learn from Arjuna.</b>

66
00:05:13.875 --> 00:05:18.583
<b>He doesn't have even a trace of ego.</b>

67
00:05:18.583 --> 00:05:21.041
<b>He's asking questions,</b>

68
00:05:21.041 --> 00:05:26.208
<b>trying to fully understand my words.</b>

69
00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:31.041
<b>His only goal is to enhance his knowledge</b>

70
00:05:31.041 --> 00:05:33.958
<b>and choose the right path.</b>

71
00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:37.583
<b>Don't get caught up in personal arguments</b>

72
00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:41.125
<b>or try to prove others wrong.</b>

73
00:05:41.125 --> 00:05:45.416
<b>If you have doubts, ask respectfully.</b>

74
00:05:45.416 --> 00:05:48.041
<b>You will surely get answers.</b>

75
00:05:48.041 --> 00:05:53.458
<b>Such respectful discussions </b>
<b>and question-answer sessions</b>

76
00:05:53.458 --> 00:05:56.083
<b>are how confusions are cleared</b>

77
00:05:56.083 --> 00:05:58.625
<b>and knowledge is gained.</b>

78
00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:04.583
<b>Arjuna</b>

79
00:06:04.583 --> 00:06:08.583
<b>is looking at the subject from his perspective</b>

80
00:06:08.583 --> 00:06:12.125
<b>and is asking the questions he has.</b>

81
00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:15.250
<b>How civilized this discussion is.</b>

82
00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.958
<b>When I'm giving my teachings, </b>

83
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:21.583
<b>Arjuna listens patiently,</b>

84
00:06:21.583 --> 00:06:24.791
<b>and when he has questions,</b>

85
00:06:24.791 --> 00:06:29.041
<b>I'm calmly trying to understand him.</b>

86
00:06:29.041 --> 00:06:32.625
<b>Both of us have only one goal:</b>

87
00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:36.000
<b>to agree on the right knowledge.</b>

88
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.125
<b>In social settings too, it's natural</b>

89
00:06:41.125 --> 00:06:44.166
<b>that in any group discussion,</b>

90
00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:48.708
<b>people will have their own perspectives</b>

91
00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:55.208
<b>and thoughts about the topic at hand.</b>

92
00:06:55.208 --> 00:06:59.750
<b>The essence of so many experiences together</b>

93
00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.708
<b>can be incredibly enlightening</b>

94
00:07:03.708 --> 00:07:08.916
<b>and helpful in finding the right solution.</b>

95
00:07:08.916 --> 00:07:10.375
<b>But</b>

96
00:07:10.375 --> 00:07:15.291
<b>how many such discussions fail?</b>

97
00:07:15.291 --> 00:07:19.750
<b>Where people can't understand</b>
<b>others' perspectives,</b>

98
00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:27.166
<b>and sometimes even conflicts arise.</b>

99
00:07:27.166 --> 00:07:29.166
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

100
00:07:29.166 --> 00:07:31.583
<b>This happens</b>

101
00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:39.708
<b>when a person is only interested in </b>
<b>proving themselves right and others wrong,</b>

102
00:07:39.708 --> 00:07:43.583
<b>when they're only eager to speak,</b>

103
00:07:43.583 --> 00:07:45.625
<b>not to listen.</b>

104
00:07:45.625 --> 00:07:47.458
<b>And then,</b>

105
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:51.875
<b>there's always someone</b>

106
00:07:51.875 --> 00:07:55.125
<b>who listens to everyone respectfully,</b>

107
00:07:55.125 --> 00:07:57.791
<b>asks questions calmly,</b>

108
00:07:57.791 --> 00:08:00.458
<b>absorbs their answers,</b>

109
00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:01.875
<b>and</b>

110
00:08:01.875 --> 00:08:08.375
<b>presents their own thoughts </b>
<b>politely when it's their turn.</b>

111
00:08:08.375 --> 00:08:10.500
<b>In a social setting,</b>

112
00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:17.958
<b>this is the right way to discuss </b>
<b>with someone, to talk to others. </b>

113
00:08:17.958 --> 00:08:23.541
<b>Where only the right knowledge is the focal point.</b>

114
00:08:23.541 --> 00:08:26.583
<b>Where you respect others,</b>

115
00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:29.166
<b>understand their perspective,</b>

116
00:08:29.166 --> 00:08:33.208
<b>and ask your questions respectfully.</b>

117
00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:34.541
<b>Such a person</b>

118
00:08:34.541 --> 00:08:39.291
<b>leaves the discussion having </b>
<b>enhanced their knowledge</b>

119
00:08:39.291 --> 00:08:44.250
<b>and having built friendly </b>
<b>relationships with others.</b>

120
00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:48.125
<b>Always keep discussions topic-centered,</b>

121
00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:50.000
<b>not personal.</b>

122
00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.166
<b>Working harmoniously with others</b>

123
00:08:59.166 --> 00:09:05.250
<b>is crucial in a professional environment.</b>

124
00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.791
<b>And for this, it's necessary</b>

125
00:09:07.791 --> 00:09:12.458
<b>to fully understand each other.</b>

126
00:09:12.458 --> 00:09:13.666
<b>But</b>

127
00:09:13.666 --> 00:09:18.208
<b>sometimes, even with the right intentions,</b>

128
00:09:18.208 --> 00:09:22.708
<b>there can be gaps in mutual communication.</b>

129
00:09:22.708 --> 00:09:24.833
<b>Misunderstandings can arise.</b>

130
00:09:24.833 --> 00:09:30.458
<b>This can happen when communication isn't clear,</b>

131
00:09:30.458 --> 00:09:31.291
<b>or</b>

132
00:09:31.291 --> 00:09:37.666
<b>when the listener misinterprets the message.</b>

133
00:09:37.666 --> 00:09:39.041
<b>Mistakes</b>

134
00:09:39.041 --> 00:09:42.208
<b>can happen on both sides.</b>

135
00:09:42.208 --> 00:09:47.958
<b>From the speaker </b>
<b>as well as the listener.</b>

136
00:09:47.958 --> 00:09:49.000
<b>In such cases,</b>

137
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:54.583
<b>the habit of seeking clarification is always helpful.</b>

138
00:09:54.583 --> 00:09:57.833
<b>It's important for the listener</b>

139
00:09:57.833 --> 00:10:02.791
<b>to ask appropriate questions if needed,</b>

140
00:10:02.791 --> 00:10:03.541
<b>but</b>

141
00:10:03.541 --> 00:10:08.958
<b>in any case, they should clearly </b>
<b>express their understanding.</b>

142
00:10:08.958 --> 00:10:10.750
<b>Similarly,</b>

143
00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:16.875
<b>it's essential for the speaker to ensure at the end</b>

144
00:10:16.875 --> 00:10:21.000
<b>that the listener has understood correctly.</b>

145
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:26.291
<b>When both sides strive for clarity,</b>

146
00:10:26.291 --> 00:10:32.541
<b>no misunderstandings will </b>
<b>arise in the communication.</b>

147
00:10:32.541 --> 00:10:36.500
<b>And when there's good mutual understanding,</b>

148
00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.250
<b>all tasks</b>

149
00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:41.333
<b>will be accomplished smoothly.</b>

